    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-upside profile of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), our premier play against Pfaadt. The combination of his leadoff status and a favorable matchup allows us to exploit a specific efficiency gap: Pfaadt\u2019s slow delivery to the plate provides a significant boost to **Pete Crow-Armstrong**\u2019s stolen base probability, a critical factor given our aggressive pursuit of the scarcest category in this 5x5 format. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (74.78) and **Yordan Alvarez** (73.61) offer elite production floors today; **Yordan Alvarez** continues to serve as our anchor, with his xwOBA of 0.458 insulating his score even against a reasonably capable arm in Warren.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical adjustments in the middle of the order. **Lars Nootbaar** (62.07) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (61.15) draw strong ratings due to favorable platoon advantages and batting order stability, while **Trea Turner** (61.16) and **Kyle Schwarber** (60.24) remain viable starts despite the tough matchup against Kirby. The most difficult bench decision involved **Carson Benge** (36.49); while his position in the #3 hole typically signals high value, the combination of a difficult SP_xERA from Harrison and a poor L/L platoon matchup forced his exclusion. He narrowly missed the 40-point floor threshold, effectively protecting our daily game-cap limit in favor of the higher-probability output from **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** and **Gary Sanchez**. \n\nBeyond the starters, we are monitoring the health of **Christian Yelich** and **Colt Keith**, both of whom remain unavailable as we look for rotation depth from the likes of **Caleb Durbin**, **Casey Schmitt**, and **Josh Smith**. We remain wary of the efficiency impact of opposing starters like Kirby, who suppresses base potential for both **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber**. The roster is currently lean; with **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** held in reserve, the team remains prioritized for high-speed, high-OBP profiles to maintain our edge in the 5x5 standings as we reach late August.",
